  ✕ Reference may mutate a value read in the same expression
    ╭─[test.lis:10:33]
  9 │   let mut data = Data{ n: 1 }
 10 │   let triple = (inspect(&data), data, bump(&data))
    ·                                 ──┬─       ──┬──
    ·                                   │          ╰── may mutate `data`
    ·                                   ╰── may see the mutated value
 11 │   let _ = triple
    ╰────
  help: Make evaluation order explicit: to read the value before `&data` runs, copy it first with `let before = data`, and to read the value after, bind the reference-taking operand to a variable first · code: [infer.reference_aliases_sibling]
